# The Mac App test copy's first launch as if on an M1 with an 8-core GPU (DM_TEST_GPU_NAME / DM_TEST_GPU_CORES) on this 2560 x 1440 screen, with Frame Generation offered as on every Mac: Recommended keeps it on and lowers
# the 3D instead: Native 2560, 3D 50%, the full picture, Frame Drops lower (t_picrec_fg_cases.h's model). This M6 draws it, so this checks the glue, not an M1's speed.
name pic_mac_firstboot_m1_fg
requires mac-app
save warlock
timeout 300
env DM_TEST_VIDEO_FIRSTBOOT=1 "DM_TEST_GPU_NAME=Apple M1" DM_TEST_GPU_CORES=8 DM_GAME_SEED=305419896

expect main_menu timeout=120
enter_game
sleep 8
screenshot m1_fg.png
system_quit
check no_red
check no_red_log
check event picture how=first mode=1 res=3 up=2 aa=1 aniso=3 color=1 s3d=4 envsh=1 shq=2 fg=1 envd=1 rt=0
check log_has "→ Recommended Native 2560, 3D 50%, environment shadows on, shadows Ultra, Frame Drops lower, Frame Generation on"
check event scale3d pct=50
check log_has "temporal scaler: .* built in"
check log_has "frame generation: interpolator .* built in"
